    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0083" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 534/20.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sherrill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Informs him that his telegram relative to Bolivia’s request for good offices in
                    Argentina was received almost at same time as similar request on behalf of
                    Argentine interests in Bolivia. Adds that the United States viewed these
                    requests as a proof of confidence of the two countries in the sincere and
                    impartial friendship of this Government, that the dual trust was uninvited and
                    was accepted in cordial friendship to both countries, and that favorable action
                    was taken on each, and simultaneous telegrams sent to the legations at Buenos
                    Aires and La Paz to this effect.</p>
            </div>
